/-!
# The inverse image of the centre on the strict transform is an effective Cartier divisor

Let `S` be a scheme, let `A` be an algebraic space over `S`, let `Z ⊆ A` be a closed subspace,
let `b : A' ⟶ A` be the blowup of `A` in `Z` and let `f : X ⟶ A` be an algebraic space over `A`.
The strict transform `X'` of `X`, a closed subspace of `X ×_A A'`, has the property that the
inverse image of `Z` along `X' ⟶ X ×_A A' ⟶ X ⟶ A` is an effective Cartier divisor on `X'`;
equivalently `X'`, with its morphism to `X`, is an object of the category `𝒞` of Stacks 085U for
the centre `f⁻¹Z`.

This is the space-level counterpart of the scheme-level
`AlgebraicGeometry.isCartierOver_strictTransform` of Stacks 080E.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isPullbackDefined_ι_of_definingIdealSheaf_eq_supportedSections`: the
  general statement, for a locally principal closed subspace `T` of an algebraic space `W` and
  the closed subspace of `W` cut out by the ideal of sections supported on `|T|`: the inverse
  image of `T` there is an effective Cartier divisor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isPullbackDefined_strictTransform_of_isBlowupAlong` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartierOver_strictTransform_of_isBlowupAlong`: **the inverse image
  of the centre on the strict transform is an effective Cartier divisor**, in the two spellings
  of Stacks 083Y and of the category `𝒞` of Stacks 085U.

## Implementation notes

The scheme-level proof presents the strict transform as the scheme-theoretic image of the affine
complement of the exceptional preimage and pulls the exceptional divisor back along that image.
No scheme-theoretic image is needed here: the statement is checked on étale charts, where it
becomes the elementary fact that the quotient of a ring by the `a`-power torsion has `a` as a
nonzerodivisor.

Three inputs do the work.  The exceptional preimage `T = pr_{A'}^{-1}(b⁻¹Z)` is locally principal
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyPrincipal_preimage`, Stacks 083X, applied to the exceptional
divisor of the blowup), so every point of an étale chart of `X ×_A A'` has an affine étale chart
`V` over it on which the defining ideal of `T` is `(a)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_affine_chart_definingIdealAt_eq_span`).  The strict transform is
honestly cut out by the ideal of sections supported on `|T|`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealSheaf_strictTransform_of_isBlowupAlong`), and on `V` that
ideal is the `a`-power torsion by Stacks 0859 (2) in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_supportedSectionsSubmodule_iff_mem_primaryComponent`.  Finally the
base change of `V` along the closed immersion of the strict transform is an affine étale chart of
the strict transform, on which the defining ideal of the inverse image of `T` is generated by the
image of `a` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_preimage_eq_map`); that image is a
nonzerodivisor because the kernel of restriction to the chart is exactly the `a`-power torsion.
Charts through every point suffice for condition (3) of Stacks 083C,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasEffectiveCartierEtalePullbacks_of_pointwise_charts`, which gives
invertibility of the ideal sheaf.

The general statement carries local principality of `T` and the identification of the closed
subspace with the ideal of supported sections as hypotheses, and nothing about blowups; for the
strict transform of a blowup both are available unconditionally, which is what the specialization
uses.

